      "username": "Reckless",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-10-14T22:06:21.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(As an aside, where exactly is it stated that F6 vs. IL is a legal game despite the usual limit of five players?&nbsp; It doesn't seem to be in the \"rulebook\" for Shattered Timelines, unless it's hidden somewhere I didn't see it.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It isn't, actually.&nbsp; Which was funny during playtesting, because it seemed like EVERYONE wanted to playtest/balance Iron Legacy against either:<br><br>A.&nbsp; The Freedom Six.<br><br>or</p>\n<p><br>B.&nbsp; Young Legacy, Finest Legacy, and Greatest Legacy.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Both are still considered outside of the normal rules for Sentinels of the Multiverse.</p>",
